// Elimination (Store/Store) -- SOURCE program.
//
// rmm-zoo property: elim_ss (Elimination / sound).
// Source: Moiseenko, Podkopaev & Koznov, "A Survey of Programming Language
//         Memory Models" (2021), Tables 1-2 -- the Elimination group;
//         Sevcik & Aspinall, "On Validity of Program Transformations in the Java
//         Memory Model" (ECOOP 2008); Sevcik's thesis, fig. 1.4.
//
// Overwritten-write elimination: the write of 1 to x is dead, being overwritten
// by the write of 2 with no intervening access to x. opt.lit is the result of
// dropping it. Sound in every model in the zoo that has an elim_ss cell.
//
// This completes the Elimination row for MoRDor: Store/Load and Load/Load are
// already covered by litmus-tests/sevcik_thesis/Redundant Read Elimination
// (f1.4)/ (RREW*, RRER*), and Load/Store by ../load-store/ here.
x := 0;
y := 0;
x := 1;
x := 2;
r1 := x;
if (r1 = 2) {
  y := 1
} else {skip}
